* vco_core_body_selft0_l1054.spice -- the campaign body including the S4-scaled inductor
* model (issue #244 stage S4). Derived from vco_core_body_selft0.spice (sha256
* e0982010f9dc2214e36f2b8d6c53e14e4af245d0ebe497202fe4ec7f4bc18192) by EXACTLY ONE edit: the .include line. selft=0 as in the campaign body.
* vco_core_body_selft0.spice -- the campaign body with VBIC self-heating switched off
* (selft=0 on XQ1..XQ4). Derived from the elaborate-post79 vco_core_body.spice
* (sha256 9ce081a6af3d5f3a884e0157e8e25a562d2afa3826b8de7c8d380ee812a6f155) by EXACTLY four
* instance-parameter additions and nothing else; the four changed lines are XQ1, XQ2, XQ3, XQ4.
*
* Why (run record 20261115-*, ../records/): ngspice-47 (runner image and dispatch host since ~2026-11-13)
* aborts this deck at the first transient timepoint -- VBIC's self-heating path hands the temperature
* limiter a NaN ("The temperature limiting function received NaN", then "Timestep too small;
* initial timepoint ... q.xq1.qnpn13g2v"). ngspice-46 passes the byte-identical deck (3/3 on the
* fleet 2026-11-05; re-measured locally 2026-11-15, f matches the record to all printed digits).
* ngspice-47p1 fails the same way. The defect is NOT the dsubw card (bare-diode probe at
* T = TNOM = 27 C prints a finite cd = 9.76683e-15 on both 46 and 47); it is the VBIC thermal path.
* selft=0 (rth = selft * 3.26e3 * (4/Nx)**0.9 -> rth = 0) disables junction self-heating.
*
* Measured bound of the deviation, this bench, tt_nominal, Vctrl = 0, 20 ns two-WHEN estimator:
*   ngspice-46 (self-heating on):  f_osc 4.21337 GHz, vdiff_pp 0.593942 V
*   ngspice-47 selft=0:            f_osc 4.21337 GHz, vdiff_pp 0.591418 V
* i.e. frequency unchanged below print precision; differential swing -0.42 %. The bound is measured
* at the 27 C anchor only; it is NOT extrapolated to hot corners, where self-heating is larger
* (bisect record 20261106-055147: at 125 C the variants separate by far more). No hot-corner number
* may come from this body.
* Applicability: anchor-1 yield campaign only (27 C, issue #244). The #50 grid and any 125 C unit
* remain governed by the pending operator decision on the dsubw card and are NOT run from here.
.include sg13g2_inductor_em_l1054.spice
